<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.KOREAN LG ELEC H1/97 NET SHARPLY RISES.</title>
<headline>S.KOREAN LG ELEC H1/97 NET SHARPLY RISES.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net				 109.6 vs    78.3</p>
<p>    Turnover			4,400.6 vs 3,676.9</p>
<p>    Profit before tax	     130.4 vs    92.3</p>
<p>    Ordinary profit		 135.4 vs    35.2</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	  5.0 (loss) vs 57.1 (gain)</p>
<p>NOTE - An official at LG Electronics Inc, a unit of the LG Group, said its profitability had improved as a result of production cost cuts including relocation of some manufacturing lines abroad. LG's share capital decreased by 2.07 million shares to 104.92 million during the 12-month period to June after it disposed of as many preferred shares it owned in May according to the board of directors' decision.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
